Subject: [PATCH] elan: retry "not ready"/"sensor busy" on 04f3:0c4f instead of failing

elan.c's CAPTURE_READ_DATA reads a one-byte status. The driver's own comments
document three values: 0x55 "finger present", 0x00 "not ready", and 0xaf
"finger removed or sensor busy". Only 0x55 is handled generally. 0x00 and 0xaf
are retried after 10 ms *for ELAN_0C58 alone*; on every other device they fall
through to FP_DEVICE_ERROR_PROTO, which is fatal to the whole operation.

On 04f3:0c4f (Acer Predator PT516-52s) that makes enrolment impossible, and it
is reproducible. Measured 2026-11-03: a stage is accepted, then a protocol
error arrives 0-5 s later while the driver is arming the next capture on a pad
the finger has just left -- exactly when the sensor reports "finger removed or
sensor busy". fprintd writes the print only on completion, so the partial
enrolment is discarded and the next attempt restarts at stage 1. Ten cycles in
44 s never reached stage 2 of 6, with 1.20-1.40 s of contact every time and the
stages themselves accepted. The one enrolment that ever succeeded on this
machine logged zero protocol errors -- i.e. the sensor happened to be ready at
each of the six transitions.

Verify is unaffected by comparison because each verify is an independent
operation: there is no accumulated state for one fault to discard. That is why
the same error rate is a nuisance to verification and fatal to enrolment.

A new unique driver_data bit is used rather than widening the ELAN_0C58 test,
so no other device changes behaviour. Every dev_type site was audited against
bit 4: ELAN_NOT_ROTATED is bit 1; the ELAN_0C42 and ELAN_0C58 tests are
equality comparisons; ELAN_CALIBRATION_ATTEMPTS keys on ELAN_0C58 and still
yields the default; the open-time switch matches only ELAN_0907; and the single
command whose .devices is not ELAN_ALL_DEV is also ELAN_0907, which stays
skipped for this device either way.

Against: libfprint v1.94.100
Context: cachyPool runbooks/fingerprint.md section 20x
---
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
index f9cc52f..3efa953 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.c
@@ -557,11 +557,13 @@ capture_run_state (FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
           fpi_image_device_report_finger_status (idev, TRUE);
           elan_run_cmd (ssm, dev, &get_image_cmd, ELAN_CMD_TIMEOUT);
         }
-      else if (self->dev_type == ELAN_0C58 && self->last_read &&
+      else if ((self->dev_type == ELAN_0C58 || self->dev_type == ELAN_0C4F) &&
+               self->last_read &&
                (self->last_read[0] == 0x00 || self->last_read[0] == 0xaf))
         {
           /* 0x00 - not ready
-           * 0xaf - finger removed or sensor busy (seen on 0x0c58) */
+           * 0xaf - finger removed or sensor busy (seen on 0x0c58, and on
+           *        0x0c4f between two enrolment stages) */
           fpi_ssm_jump_to_state_delayed (ssm, CAPTURE_WAIT_FINGER, 10);
         }
       else
diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
index 6bbaae0..5fd4baa 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/elan.h
@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@
 #define ELAN_0C03 (1 << 1)
 #define ELAN_0C42 (1 << 2)
 #define ELAN_0C58 (1 << 3)
+/* answers 0x00 "not ready" / 0xaf "finger removed or sensor busy"
+ * between captures; those must be retried, not reported as a protocol
+ * error, or an enrolment cannot survive the gap between two stages */
+#define ELAN_0C4F (1 << 4)
 
 /* devices which don't require frame rotation before assembling */
 #define ELAN_NOT_ROTATED ELAN_0C03
@@ -220,7 +224,7 @@ static const FpIdEntry elan_id_table[] = {
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c42, .driver_data = ELAN_0C42},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c4b, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c4d, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
-  {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c4f, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
+  {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c4f, .driver_data = ELAN_0C4F},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c63, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c6e, .driver_data = ELAN_ALL_DEV},
   {.vid = ELAN_VEND_ID,  .pid = 0x0c58, .driver_data = ELAN_0C58},
